{"phase":"post","id":"toolu_01R7z53fmJ5LA61PzvPFSnKk","tool":"WebSearch","result":"{\"query\":\"ChatGPT \\\"Dot\\\" feature OR product 2026\",\"results\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"srvtoolu_01DADNVSqSLPzb6Lt6wcRBbk\",\"content\":[{\"title\":\"OpenAI launches Dots that keep working without user prompts\",\"url\":\"https://www.medianama.com/2026/10/223-openai-launches-dots-devday-2026/\"},{\"title\":\"OpenAI Dots and Email: What a Dot Can Do With Your Inbox (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://www.dragapp.com/blog/openai-dots/\"},{\"title\":\"ChatGPT\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ChatGPT\"},{\"title\":\"OpenAI Dots: Always-On ChatGPT Agents Explained\",\"url\":\"https://www.relevantaudience.com/ai/openai-dots-always-on-agents-chatgpt/\"},{\"title\":\"OpenAI Dots Explained: ChatGPT Dots Guide (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://codersera.com/blog/openai-chatgpt-dots-guide-2026/\"},{\"title\":\"A Guide to ChatGPT Dots: How OpenAI's Always-On Agents Work\",\"url\":\"https://composio.dev/content/a-guide-to-chatgpt-dots-how-openai-s-always-on-agents-work\"},{\"title\":\"OpenAI Dots: Always-On Agents in ChatGPT, Explained\",\"url\":\"https://www.datacamp.com/blog/openai-dots\"},{\"title\":\"ChatGPT Updates by OpenAI - October 2026 - Releasebot\",\"url\":\"https://releasebot.io/updates/openai/chatgpt\"},{\"title\":\"ChatGPT Atlas\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ChatGPT_Atlas\"}]},\"Here's what I found on OpenAI's \\\"Dots\\\" feature in ChatGPT:\\n\\n## What are ChatGPT Dots?\\n\\nAt DevDay 2026, OpenAI introduced dots: persistent AI agents powered by GPT-6 Astra, that operate independently in the cloud and continue tasks without user prompts. OpenAI launched dots on 29 September 2026: always-on agents in ChatGPT, powered by GPT-6 Astra, that each run on their own cloud computer and keep working toward a user's goals 24/7.\\n\\n## Key Capabilities\\n- Each dot runs on GPT-6 Astra with its own cloud computer and browser, and OpenAI says it can connect to over 4,000 apps through plugins.\\n- A dot is a named, avatar-style agent inside ChatGPT that takes ongoing responsibility for work you hand it and keeps making progress when you are not talking to it — researching in the background, running scheduled jobs like a daily calendar review, messaging you in Slack when it needs a decision, and handing coding work to Codex.\\n- A dot can monitor customer feedback, implement and test minor fixes, and submit pull requests with video documentation.\\n- They are powered by GPT-6 Astra, and you control them with Custom Rules that decide which actions need your approval.\\n\\n## Availability and Pricing\\n- At launch, dots are available on ChatGPT Pro outside the EEA, Switzerland and the UK, on Business Premium in all supported regions, and in beta on Enterprise, Edu and Healthcare once an admin turns them on.\\n- Dots are not free: your first dot is included with ChatGPT Pro (from $100/month) or Business Premium, and you must be 18+.\\n- The first dot is included in Pro and Business Premium at no extra cost, and conversations with it do not count toward ChatGPT usage limits.\\n- As for future pricing, OpenAI says users will later be able to add more dots and scale each one by speed or monthly workload.\\n\\n## Setup\\nYou create your first dot in the ChatGPT desktop app or ChatGPT on desktop web, follow the onboarding prompts, connect your apps, and let it introduce itself.\\n\\n## How It Differs from Previous ChatGPT Agent Features\\nEarlier ChatGPT agent features ran a task when you asked, then stopped. In contrast, a dot is persistent — it's not just ChatGPT that keeps running after you close the window; the bigger change is persistent responsibility.\\n\\nThis appears to be a genuinely new, very recently launched (late September/early October 2026) feature rather than something from my existing knowledge base, so this search was necessary to provide accurate, current details.\"],\"durationSeconds\":10.460028875,\"searchCount\":1}"}
{"phase":"post","id":"toolu_015ztZ3UnVf4x79asLJ82bB9","tool":"WebSearch","result":"{\"query\":\"Meta \\\"Muse\\\" AI agent assistant 2026\",\"results\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"srvtoolu_01JoAUG1XajG7xjiJKjN2o5T\",\"content\":[{\"title\":\"Meta Announces Muse AI Agent for Personal Tasks and Organization - Bloomberg\",\"url\":\"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-09-08/meta-announces-muse-ai-agent-for-personal-tasks-and-organization\"},{\"title\":\"Meta's Muse agent is attacking one of the economy's most profitable weak spots\",\"url\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/09/27/meta-muse-ai-personal-agent.html\"},{\"title\":\"Muse (AI agent)\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muse_(AI_agent)\"},{\"title\":\"Meta is expanding its AI agent Muse to small businesses\",\"url\":\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/09/29/meta-is-expanding-its-ai-agent-muse-to-small-businesses/\"},{\"title\":\"Meta debuts its Muse AI agent. Will consumers trust it?\",\"url\":\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/09/08/meta-debuts-its-muse-ai-agent-will-consumers-trust-it/\"},{\"title\":\"Meta AI\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meta_AI\"},{\"title\":\"Introducing Muse: The World’s First Personal AI Agent Built for Everyone\",\"url\":\"https://about.fb.com/news/2026/09/introducing-muse-personal-ai-agent/\"},{\"title\":\"Meta Muse Guide 2026: AI Agent App, Pricing & Mac\",\"url\":\"https://codersera.com/blog/meta-muse-ai-agent-app-guide-2026/\"},{\"title\":\"Meta Launches Muse AI Agent: $20 and $100 Tiers [2026]\",\"url\":\"https://tech-insider.org/meta-muse-personal-ai-agent-launch-2026/\"}]},\"Here's what I found on Meta's \\\"Muse\\\" AI agent:\\n\\n## Overview\\nMuse is an artificial intelligence agent developed by Meta Platforms, announced on 8 September 2026, described as a personal AI agent capable of carrying out long-running tasks on a user's behalf, rather than answering queries in a single exchange as a chatbot does. The agent shares its name with the series of models Meta's AI lab is developing and can help automate a variety of tasks, including online shopping, buying movie tickets, scheduling appointments, or filling out a permission slip for a class field trip.\\n\\n## Leadership & Technology\\nMuse was developed under Alexandr Wang, whom Meta appointed as its first chief AI officer after acquiring a 49% stake in Scale AI for $14.3 billion in June 2025. It runs on the latest generation of Meta's models, developed under Wang; the first of these, Muse Spark, was introduced in April 2026. Muse Spark is a multimodal reasoning model designed for tasks including tool use, visual reasoning, and multi-agent workflows.\\n\\n## Key Features\\nAccording to Meta's official announcement, Muse is a secure, private personal AI agent that proactively helps with people's goals and suggests ideas, running on Muse Secure VM, a dedicated virtual machine that houses both the agent and a person's data. Once a person shares a goal with Muse, it helps them develop a personalized plan and coordinate their time and resources, then advances the work on its own — it can open a browser, fill out forms, and negotiate on their behalf.\\n\\nThe agent connects broadly across a user's digital life — it works by connecting to apps and services that are part of everyday workflows, like email, calendars, payments, and apps for health and fitness, the smart home, dining, shopping, music and events, and more.\\n\\nAdditional capabilities announced in late September include a Realtime Avatar model allowing video conversations with a visual representation of the agent, the ability to control applications on macOS, an email address of its own, and the ability to work with Meta's smart glasses through a wake word.\\n\\n## Availability & Pricing\\nThe rollout arrives in the US first, restricted to users 18 and older, pushing Meta further into a race against OpenAI, Google, and Microsoft over who controls the AI agent that acts on a person's behalf rather than just answering questions. Muse launched in the US on September 8, 2026 for users 18 and older, with a free tier plus Power ($20/month) and Maximum ($100/month) paid tiers; a native Mac client followed on September 17, and by September 23 Muse had crossed 2.5 million US downloads according to Sensor Tower.\\n\\n## Bus…"}
